;; ci's divergences from gcc 15.2 (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: C5 (write-ahead)"; doc/c/SPEC.md §12.5, §13, §14):
;; the classes every program of bin/ci check that does not pass falls into, each with why it is by design or
;; deferred and where that was decided, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A program's class is the first
;; whose :match finds its result and reason ("RESULT REASON", as test/c/check-linux-amd64.edn writes them; a
;; program of test/c/check-known.edn fails with "known REASON (...)"). bin/ci divergences judges the recorded
;; check against them. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :by-design
  :title "read and printed, out of eval (SPEC §14)"
  :kind :design
  :why "GNU nested functions, inline assembly, vector types, __real__ and __imag__, the decimal and _Float16/_Float128 types: CS3 (a)'s list"
  :decided "SPEC §14, CS3 (a)"
  :match [#"^refused by-design: " #"^fail known asm: " #"^read-refused literal: convert: floating suffix d"]}
 {:id :long-double
  :title "long double is double (CS35)"
  :kind :design
  :why "the user's decision of 2026-10-28: no software x87 arithmetic; a program that declares or converts to long double and differs from gcc's run"
  :decided "CS35, SPEC §12.5"
  :match [#"^fail differ (status 134 \(gcc 0\)|stdout) uses-long-double$" #"^refused checker: main: _Generic without a chosen association uses-long-double$"]}
 {:id :speed
  :title "speed: programs beyond the check's 10 s"
  :kind :design
  :why "an interpreter of nodes is 10 to 100 times slower than gcc's code (goi's class of the same name)"
  :decided "CS107 (a); GOI-SPEC §11.1's rule"
  :match [#"^fail differ status timeout"]}
 {:id :ub
  :title "undefined behaviour the reference's runs show (SPEC §13.2)"
  :kind :design
  :why "a program reading uninitialized or out-of-bounds memory, whose result is the layout's and the stack's: gcc's -O0 and -O2 runs differ, or the value is the reference's memory"
  :decided "CS10 (a), SPEC §13.2"
  :match [#"^fail known ub: "]}
 {:id :missing-builtin
  :title "a builtin ci does not implement yet (deferred)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the program calls a gcc builtin ci's back end has no implementation of: the run faults on the undefined function; a gap ci closes builtin by builtin (queue 122, finding 2: gcc-builtin took them as by design). Since queue 154 only __builtin_va_arg_pack is left (va-arg-pack-1.c: it forwards an always_inline function's variadic arguments, which needs a frame to keep them; ci never inlines); queue 154 built __builtin_popcountg and the type-generic bit builtins, __builtin_stdc_*, __builtin_*_overflow_p, __builtin_clear_padding, __builtin_assoc_barrier, __builtin_isinff and the f/l spellings, __atomic_is_lock_free"
  :decided "the user, 2026-11-02 (queue 122, F2)"
  :match [#"^fail differ status 139 .*undefined function __(builtin|atomic)"]}
 {:id :gcc-builtin
  :title "gcc's own semantics of a builtin a program redefines"
  :kind :design
  :why "gcc expands a call of a library builtin (llabs, ...) itself even where the program defines the function; ci calls the program's definition, as the standard says"
  :decided "SPEC §7.9, CS264 (a)"
  :match [#"^fail known gcc-builtin: "]}
 {:id :abi
  :title "gcc's layout options the forms do not carry"
  :kind :design
  :why "-mms-bitfields and similar target options change layout; the reference's runs were made with them, ci lays out by the psABI"
  :decided "SPEC §12.3, CS264 (a)"
  :match [#"^fail known abi: "]}
 ;; a guard class since 2026-11-06 (CS106's structures): no program of the corpora is refused or fails with a VLA today
 {:id :vla
  :title "variably modified types beyond those built (deferred)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "block-scope VLAs, their storage freed (C6.1); since queue 165 the variably modified types of declarations, typedefs, parameters (their sizes evaluated at entry), casts, typeof and sizeof; since 2026-11-06 GNU's structures and unions with variably modified members, laid out at run time where their definition stands (offsets, size, sizeof, offsetof, members, copies, va_arg's by reference, an empty initializer: CS106). Left: a bit-field after a member of variable size, a member of variable size in an anonymous member, a VLA aligned beyond 16, a parameter of a structure type of variable size"
  :decided "CS106"
  :match [#"^refused vla: " #"^fail known vla: " #"^fail differ status 139 .*fault: stack overflow \(alloca\)"]}
 ;; a guard class since 2026-11-06 (CS105's complex integers built): it holds the complex types of wide parts
 {:id :complex-int
  :title "GNU's complex types of wide integer parts (deferred)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the floating complex types and since 2026-11-06 GNU's complex integer types of at most 64-bit parts (tree-complex.cc's lowering, the parts' arithmetic in the part type) are built (CS105); a complex of __int128 or _BitInt(N > 64) parts is refused; a complex of _Float16, _Float128 or a decimal type is by design (SPEC §14, the class by-design)"
  :decided "CS105"
  :match [#"^refused complex: "]}
 {:id :read
  :title "repr/c's reader's known gaps (deferred)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a declaration that begins in one file and ends in another, a main file that includes itself: refused by the converter (C3b's classes, test/repr/c/roundtrip-known.edn)"
  :decided "C3b.2, CS104; self-include CS261 (a)"
  :match [#"^read-refused (split-declaration|self-include): "]}
 {:id :checker
  :title "the checker's own differences ci meets (deferred, CS93 (a))"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a type or constant the checker computes otherwise than gcc: fixed as ci meets them (CS93 (a)), the rest listed in test/c/check-known.edn"
  :decided "CS93 (a)"
  :match [#"^fail known checker: "]}
 {:id :threads
  :title "threads (deferred)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "pthread_create needs musl's clone (assembly) as a native over goroutines (§6.5's plan): C6"
  :decided "§6.5, CS264 (a)"
  :match [#"^fail known threads: " #"^fail differ status 139 .*undefined function __clone"]}
 {:id :fenv
  :title "floating-point exception flags and signaling NaNs are not modelled (C7)"
  :kind :design
  :why "a program that raises FE_INVALID on a signaling NaN (-fsignaling-nans) and tests fetestexcept: ci's arithmetic keeps no flags (SPEC §12.5)"
  :decided "C7 (write-ahead), CS130"
  :match [#"^fail known fenv: "]}
 ;; a guard class since 2026-11-06: no program of the corpora is in it
 {:id :signals
  :title "a signal delivered to the program's handler (review 006)"
  :kind :gap
  :why "since 2026-11-06 a synchronous fault (SIGFPE, SIGSEGV) is delivered where it is raised to the handler sigaction or signal installed (crt's Raise and SyncHook, Sys.SyncSignal: not when SIG_DFL, SIG_IGN, blocked or already running), and kill, tkill and tgkill deliver to handlers as before; a handler that returns from a fault ends the run with the fault (the machine would raise it forever), SIGILL's traps are not delivered, and one program's hook is the process's (a REPL's latest program)"
  :decided "CS191 (a); review 006"
  :match [#"^fail known signals: "]}
 {:id :complit-static
  :title "compound literals with storage class specifiers: the builder's places (C7 follow-up)"
  :kind :gap
  :why "C23 6.5.3.6: (static T) {...} and (register T) {...} (file scope and block scope, with goto re-entry): ci's builder places them as automatic objects, c23-complit-2 faults at its first use"
  :decided "C7 follow-up, CS131"
  :match [#"^fail known complit-static: "]}
 ;; a guard class: no program of the corpora gives -I- today; it holds CS239 (a)'s refusal when one does (queue 122, F9)
 {:id :refused-option
  :title "an option whose effect the read does not model (-I-)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "-I- splits the include search into the quote and the bracket chains; the read refuses a file that gives it instead of running it on a wrong search order (CS239 (a); modelling the split is CS239 (b))"
  :decided "CS239 (a)"
  :match [#"^read-refused option: option "]}
]
